      "description": [
        "A thiamine phosphate that is thiamine(1+) in which the hydroxy group has been replaced by a diphosphate group. It is the active form of vitamin B<small><sub>1</sub></small> and an essential cofactor for enzymes in key metabolic pathways."
      ],
